593601.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australia-moves-to-tax-meta-google-tiktok-to-fund-newsrooms/articleshow/130593601.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australia-moves-to-tax-meta-google-tiktok-to-fund-newsrooms/articleshow/130593601.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-04-29T07:09:51+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-130593597,imgsize-9138.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['She’s guilty of something': Candace Owens faces intense scrutiny following show cancellations and viral posts]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/130592843.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Candace Owens is trending after canceling recent shows, with a viral post raising unverified claims about her absence. The post suggests possible connections to a recent incident, but no credible evidence supports these allegations. Owens has not responded publicly, fueling further speculation online. As the story spreads, it highlights how quickly social media narratives can grow despite a lack of confirmed facts.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/shes-guilty-of-something-candace-owens-faces-intense-scrutiny-following-show-cancellations-and-viral-posts/articleshow/130592843.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/shes-guilty-of-something-candace-owens-faces-intense-scrutiny-following-show-cancellations-and-viral-posts/articleshow/130592843.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-04-29T05:24:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Barsha Dutta</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-130592843,imgsize-29608.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Candace Owens and Cole Allen claims explode online as White House Correspondents Dinner questions raise deeper mystery]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/130592345.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Viral posts on X claim a connection between Candace Owens and Cole Allen, but there is no verified evidence. The claims rely on unrelated links and speculation. No official source or news outlet has confirmed any investigation. At this point, the story is based on online rumors, not facts, and should be treated with caution.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/candace-owens-and-cole-allen-claims-explode-online-as-white-house-correspondents-dinner-questions-raise-deeper-mystery/articleshow/130592345.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/candace-owens-and-cole-allen-claims-explode-online-as-white-house-correspondents-dinner-questions-raise-deeper-mystery/articleshow/130592345.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-04-29T03:53:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sehjal Gupta</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-130592375,imgsize-675051.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Doja Cat issues apology after Twitch mods ban PlaqueBoyMax unexpectedly]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/130590102.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Doja Cat faced a Twitch controversy after moderators banned a supportive viewer, PlaqueBoyMax, during her live stream.  The rapper clarified on X that the ban was not her decision and she was unhappy with her moderation team's actions. She promised to review her mods to prevent similar incidents, emphasizing fairness for her viewers.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/doja-cat-issues-apology-after-twitch-mods-ban-plaqueboymax-unexpectedly/articleshow/130590102.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/doja-cat-issues-apology-after-twitch-mods-ban-plaqueboymax-unexpectedly/articleshow/130590102.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-04-29T02:00:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sumit Roy</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-130590093,imgsize-755585.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Texas daycare accused of H-1B scam; visas tied to unrelated job roles]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/130590164.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/texas-daycare-accused-of-h-1b-scam-in-pay-to-play-scheme-visas-tied-to-unrelated-job-roles/articleshow/130590164.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/texas-daycare-accused-of-h-1b-scam-in-pay-to-play-scheme-visas-tied-to-unrelated-job-roles/articleshow/130590164.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-04-29T02:34:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-130590193,imgsize-110610.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Silent operations to nuclear balance: The secret spy networks that quietly shaped the Cold War]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/130590178.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Cold War was shaped not just by leaders and weapons, but by vast intelligence networks that gathered and shared crucial information. From spies and defectors to surveillance technology and allied cooperation, these systems reduced uncertainty, influenced key decisions and helped prevent nuclear escalation, quietly steering the conflict through knowledge rather than direct confrontation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/silent-operations-to-nuclear-balance-the-secret-spy-networks-that-quietly-shaped-the-cold-war/articleshow/130590178.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/silent-operations-to-nuclear-balance-the-secret-spy-networks-that-quietly-shaped-the-cold-war/articleshow/130590178.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-04-29T02:33:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-130590184,imgsize-1550625.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bizarre tax laws in US could drain 30+ nations’ World Cup earnings as FIFA fails to secure exemption]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/130589917.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The 2026 FIFA World Cup faces an unexpected financial divide as US tax laws and uneven international treaties mean teams will be taxed differently on tournament earnings. While FIFA holds tax-exempt status, many federations do not, leaving non-European nations particularly exposed. With varying state taxes and limited exemptions, the expanded 48-team format risks creating major economic disparities between participants.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/international-sports/bizarre-tax-laws-in-us-could-drain-30-nations-world-cup-earnings-as-fifa-fails-to-secure-exemption/articleshow/130589917.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/international-sports/bizarre-tax-laws-in-us-could-drain-30-nations-world-cup-earnings-as-fifa-fails-to-secure-exemption/articleshow/130589917.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-04-29T02:03:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.